  26:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****                       ##### DAC Peripheral features #####
  27:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****   ==============================================================================
  28:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     [..]        
  29:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       *** DAC Channels ***
  30:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       ====================  
  31:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     [..]  
ARM GAS  C:\Users\24705\AppData\Local\Temp\ccIDpHTN.s 			page 2


  32:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     STM32F0 devices integrates no, one or two 12-bit Digital Analog Converters.
  33:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     STM32F05x devices have one converter (channel1)
  34:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     STM32F07x & STM32F09x devices have two converters (i.e. channel1 & channel2)
  35:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c **** 
  36:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     When 2 converters are present (i.e. channel1 & channel2)  they 
  37:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     can be used independently or simultaneously (dual mode):
  38:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       (#) DAC channel1 with DAC_OUT1 (PA4) as output
  39:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       (#) DAC channel2 with DAC_OUT2 (PA5) as output
  40:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       
  41:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       *** DAC Triggers ***
  42:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       ====================
  43:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     [..]
  44:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     Digital to Analog conversion can be non-triggered using DAC_TRIGGER_NONE
  45:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     and DAC_OUT1/DAC_OUT2 is available once writing to DHRx register. 
  46:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     [..] 
  47:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     Digital to Analog conversion can be triggered by:
  48:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       (#) External event: EXTI Line 9 (any GPIOx_PIN_9) using DAC_TRIGGER_EXT_IT9.
  49:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****           The used pin (GPIOx_PIN_9) must be configured in input mode.
  50:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****   
  51:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       (#) Timers TRGO: TIM2, TIM3, TIM6, and TIM15 
  52:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****           (DAC_TRIGGER_T2_TRGO, DAC_TRIGGER_T3_TRGO...)
  53:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****   
  54:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       (#) Software using DAC_TRIGGER_SOFTWARE
  55:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****   
  56:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       *** DAC Buffer mode feature ***
  57:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       =============================== 
  58:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       [..] 
  59:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       Each DAC channel integrates an output buffer that can be used to 
  60:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       reduce the output impedance, and to drive external loads directly
  61:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       without having to add an external operational amplifier.
  62:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       To enable, the output buffer use  
  63:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       sConfig.DAC_OutputBuffer = DAC_OUTPUTBUFFER_ENABLE;
  64:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       [..]           
  65:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       (@) Refer to the device datasheet for more details about output 
  66:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****           impedance value with and without output buffer.
  67:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c **** 
  68:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       *** GPIO configurations guidelines ***
  69:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       =====================
  70:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       [..] 
  71:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       When a DAC channel is used (ex channel1 on PA4) and the other is not 
  72:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       (ex channel1 on PA5 is configured in Analog and disabled).
  73:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       Channel1 may disturb channel2 as coupling effect.
  74:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       Note that there is no coupling on channel2 as soon as channel2 is turned on.
  75:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       Coupling on adjacent channel could be avoided as follows:
  76:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       when unused PA5 is configured as INPUT PULL-UP or DOWN. 
  77:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       PA5 is configured in ANALOG just before it is turned on.     
  78:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****             
  79:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        *** DAC wave generation feature ***
  80:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        =================================== 
  81:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        [..]     
  82:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        Both DAC channels can be used to generate
  83:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****          (#) Noise wave 
  84:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****          (#) Triangle wave
  85:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****             
  86:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        *** DAC data format ***
  87:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        =======================
  88:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        [..]   
ARM GAS  C:\Users\24705\AppData\Local\Temp\ccIDpHTN.s 			page 3


  89:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        The DAC data format can be:
  90:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****          (#) 8-bit right alignment using DAC_ALIGN_8B_R
  91:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****          (#) 12-bit left alignment using DAC_ALIGN_12B_L
  92:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****          (#) 12-bit right alignment using DAC_ALIGN_12B_R
  93:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****   
  94:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        *** DAC data value to voltage correspondence ***  
  95:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        ================================================ 
  96:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        [..] 
  97:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        The analog output voltage on each DAC channel pin is determined
  98:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        by the following equation: 
  99:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        [..]
 100:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        DAC_OUTx = VREF+ * DOR / 4095
 101:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        (+) with  DOR is the Data Output Register
 102:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        [..]
 103:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****           VEF+ is the input voltage reference (refer to the device datasheet)
 104:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        [..]
 105:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****         e.g. To set DAC_OUT1 to 0.7V, use
 106:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        (+) Assuming that VREF+ = 3.3V, DAC_OUT1 = (3.3 * 868) / 4095 = 0.7V
 107:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****   
 108:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        *** DMA requests  ***
 109:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        =====================
 110:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        [..]    
 111:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        A DMA1 request can be generated when an external trigger (but not
 112:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        a software trigger) occurs if DMA1 requests are enabled using
 113:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        HAL_DAC_Start_DMA()
 114:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        [..]
 115:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        DMA1 requests are mapped as following:
 116:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****          (#) DAC channel1 : mapped on DMA1 channel3 which must be 
 117:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****              already configured
 118:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****          (#) DAC channel2 : mapped on DMA1 channel4 which must be 
 119:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****              already configured
 120:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****        
 121:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     (@) For Dual mode and specific signal (Triangle and noise) generation please 
 122:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****         refer to Extended Features Driver description        
 123:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****         STM32F0 devices with one channel (one converting capability) does not
 124:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****         support Dual mode and specific signal (Triangle and noise) generation.
 125:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       
 126:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****                       ##### How to use this driver #####
 127:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****   ==============================================================================
 128:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****     [..]          
 129:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       (+) DAC APB clock must be enabled to get write access to DAC
 130:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****           registers using HAL_DAC_Init()
 131:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       (+) Configure DAC_OUTx (DAC_OUT1: PA4, DAC_OUT2: PA5) in analog mode.
 132:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       (+) Configure the DAC channel using HAL_DAC_ConfigChannel() function.
 133:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       (+) Enable the DAC channel using HAL_DAC_Start() or HAL_DAC_Start_DMA() functions.
