 198:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       By default, after the HAL_DAC_Init and if the state is HAL_DAC_STATE_RESET
 199:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       all callbacks are reset to the corresponding legacy weak (surcharged) functions.
 200:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit callbacks that are respectively
 201:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       reset to the legacy weak (surcharged) functions in the HAL_DAC_Init 
 202:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_dac.c ****       and  HAL_DAC_DeInit only when these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
